---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import StatBand from "../components/StatBand.astro";
import { getSegments, loadCorridors, namedLandManagers, networkTotals } from "../lib/network";
import { formatMiles } from "../lib/format";

const segments = getSegments();
const corridors = loadCorridors();
const totals = networkTotals(segments);
const managers = namedLandManagers(segments);
const byId = new Map(segments.map((segment) => [segment.id, segment]));
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The plan"
  description="Trails to the Patching Lake and Heckman Lake cabins first, then the rest of the island — with honest land ownership and what each gap actually needs."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="The plan"
    title="Cabins first, then the rest of the island"
    lede="Four routes, in order. The first one is already being walked with a handheld and a roll of flagging. The others are further out, and the map says so."
  />

  <StatBand
    stats={[
      { value: totals.existingMi.toFixed(0), label: "Miles you can walk today" },
      { value: totals.gapMi.toFixed(0), label: "Miles still to cut", accent: true },
      { value: String(corridors.length), label: "Routes on the list" },
      { value: String(managers.length), label: "Outfits that own the ground" },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="shell py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why the cabins</p>
      <h2 class="headline mt-4 text-[length:var(--text-display-md)]">
        Three cabins are already built. Two of them you cannot walk to.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
        The Forest Service maintains cabins at Heckman Lake, on the southeast shore of Heckman
        Lake, and at Patching Lake. The Naha River trail carries you six miles from tidewater to
        the first one. The other two are float-plane country, which means the weather decides
        who gets in — and worse, who gets out. A ceiling drops, a lake freezes over in
        November, and a booked cabin becomes a problem instead of a plan.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
        A trail around the south shore and over the low divide fixes that with tread instead of
        avgas. It puts all three cabins on boot leather, gives a party a way to walk out that
        does not depend on a floatplane, and opens goat country above <span class="hydro"
          >Patching Lake</span
        > that almost nobody sets foot in now. Same ground, same cabins, better odds.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-contour/60 bg-sheet-raised py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2 class="headline text-[length:var(--text-display-md)]">The list</h2>
      <ol class="mt-12 grid gap-6">
        {
          corridors.map((corridor, index) => {
            const members = corridor.segmentIds
              .map((id) => byId.get(id))
              .filter((segment): segment is NonNullable<typeof segment> => Boolean(segment));
            return (
              <li id={corridor.id} class="card reveal scroll-mt-24 p-6 md:p-8">
                <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.5fr_1fr] lg:gap-12">
                  <div>
                    <p class="eyebrow">
                      {index === 0 ? "First project" : `Route ${String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}`}
                    </p>
                    <h3 class="headline mt-3 text-2xl md:text-3xl">{corridor.name}</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink/85">{corridor.blurb}</p>

                    <ol class="mt-6 divide-y divide-contour/40 border-y border-contour/40">
                      {members.map((segment) => (
                        <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1 py-2.5">
                          <a
                            href={`/network/${segment.id}`}
                            class="text-sm text-ink underline-offset-4 hover:underline hover:decoration-flagging"
                          >
                            {segment.name}
                          </a>
                          <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-tide">
                            {segment.status === "proposed" ? "to cut" : segment.status} ·{" "}
                            {formatMiles(segment.lengthMi)}
                          </span>
                        </li>
                      ))}
                    </ol>
                  </div>

                  <div class="flex flex-col justify-between gap-6 border-t border-contour/50 pt-6 lg:border-l lg:border-t-0 lg:pl-8 lg:pt-0">
                    <div>
                      <p class="font-display text-[length:var(--text-stat)] font-bold leading-none tracking-tight">
                        {corridor.percentComplete.toFixed(0)}<span class="text-2xl">%</span>
                      </p>
                      <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-tide">
                        {corridor.existingMi.toFixed(1)} of {corridor.totalMi.toFixed(1)} mi walkable
                      </p>
                      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-flagging-deep">
                        {corridor.gapMi.toFixed(1)} mi still to cut
                      </p>
                    </div>
                    <a
                      href={`/network?corridor=${corridor.id}`}
                      class="btn btn-outline !min-h-11 !px-5 !text-sm"
                    >
                      Walk it on the map
                    </a>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </li>
            );
          })
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell grid gap-12 py-16 md:py-24 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
    <div class="reveal">
      <h2 class="headline text-[length:var(--text-display-md)]">Nobody cuts before the study</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
        A trail on federal ground is not a weekend with a brush saw. It starts with a finished
        alignment walked on foot, then an environmental analysis with the Ketchikan–Misty Fjords
        Ranger District. Fish, deer winter range, cultural sites, wetlands. That review decides
        where tread can go and where it cannot, and it happens before anything gets cut.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
        Then it is real work: brushing the corridor, puncheon across the muskeg so the tread does
        not become a ditch, bridging what needs bridging, and tent platforms where a party would
        want to stop for the night.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <h2 class="headline text-[length:var(--text-display-md)]">Why pink means pink</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
        Pink is flagging tape — what a crew hangs on a line that does not exist yet. On this site
        it only shows up on ground nobody has cut and on the button that asks for your name.
        Nothing else.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
        Every proposed line says out loud that it has not been surveyed. Show a district ranger a
        hand-drawn route dressed up as an engineered one and you get exactly one meeting.
      </p>
      <a href="/network?view=list" class="btn btn-outline mt-8">Every segment, listed</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="on-dark bg-ink py-16 text-sheet md:py-20">
    <div class="shell max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Money</p>
      <h2 class="headline mt-4 text-[length:var(--text-display-md)]">
        There is nowhere to put a dollar yet
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-sheet/85">
        This is an informal group. No entity, no bank account, nothing tax-deductible, and Alaska
        wants an organization registered with the Department of Law before it solicits at all. So
        we are not going to pretend otherwise with a donate button.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-sheet/85">
        None of this is legal advice, and the group should get some before it takes a dollar. The
        two normal roads are incorporating as an Alaska nonprofit and filing IRS Form 1023-EZ, or
        working under a fiscal sponsor in the meantime. Until one of those exists, the useful
        thing you can give is your name and a Saturday.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/#sign-on" class="btn btn-primary">Sign on</a>
        <a href="/get-involved" class="btn btn-outline">Get on the crew list</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
